---
import MarketingLayout from '~/layouts/MarketingLayout.astro';
import Band from '~/components/ui/Band.astro';
import Card from '~/components/ui/Card.astro';
import CtaBand from '~/components/sections/CtaBand.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/site';

const beliefs = [
  {
    title: 'Narrow beats broad',
    body: 'A tool that does one thing completely is worth more than a platform that does nine things adequately. We would rather ship the fifth good tool than the first adequate platform.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Show the working',
    body: 'Any number a product shows you should be traceable to the thing that produced it. A forecast you cannot interrogate is a guess with better typography.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Your data is yours',
    body: 'Products run against your own database wherever that is possible. Where hosted processing genuinely helps, it is opt-in, scoped to the minimum, and described in plain language.',
  },
  {
    title: 'No lock-in',
    body: 'If one of our products stops being the best option for you, leaving should cost nothing but the export. We would rather earn the renewal than engineer the switching cost.',
  },
];
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="About"
  description="SimplifyBase is a product studio building focused software for commerce, operations and customer workflows."
>
  <section class="border-b border-line">
    <div class="container-page pt-16 pb-14 sm:pt-24 sm:pb-20">
      <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col items-start gap-6">
        <p class="text-eyebrow">About</p>
        <h1 class="text-display">A product studio, not a platform</h1>
        <p class="max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
          SimplifyBase builds and maintains a small family of focused tools for
          commerce and operations teams. Five products, each solving one problem
          completely, each priced on its own.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Band>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why we started</h2>
      <p>
        Every operations team we have worked with runs on a spreadsheet that
        somebody built years ago and nobody fully understands any more. It
        works, mostly. It also quietly costs the business money in ways that
        never show up in a report — the reorder that was placed too late, the
        capital sitting in stock that stopped moving in March, the payout that
        never quite reconciled.
      </p>
      <p>
        The software that exists to replace those spreadsheets tends to have the
        opposite problem. It can do everything, which means learning it is a
        project, and using it is somebody's job rather than somebody's two
        minutes.
      </p>
      <p>
        We think there is a gap between those two. That gap is what
        SimplifyBase builds for: tools that fit into the day someone already
        has, do one job properly, and can be understood by the person using
        them.
      </p>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        Products are built one at a time and maintained indefinitely. Nothing
        here is a weekend project waiting to be abandoned — if we ship it, we
        version it, document it and support it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Documentation is written when a feature is built, not when someone
        complains. That is a deliberately annoying rule and it is the reason the
        docs are worth reading.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before anything ships we ask one question: does this make the product
        better at the one thing it does, or does it make the product bigger?
        Bigger is easy to sell and hard to undo.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <Band divider eyebrow="What we believe" heading="Four things we will not trade away">
    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        beliefs.map((b) => (
          <Card class="reveal">
            <h3 class="text-title">{b.title}</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{b.body}</p>
          </Card>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </Band>

  <Band divider eyebrow="The team" heading="Small, and staying that way">
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        SimplifyBase is a small team of engineers and operators who have spent
        most of their careers inside commerce businesses rather than adjacent to
        them. Most of the problems the products solve are ones we have had
        ourselves.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are not looking to grow headcount faster than we can maintain what we
        have already shipped. That constraint is the reason the product family
        is five and not fifteen.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to talk to us — about a product, a problem, or something we
        have got wrong — <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> reaches
        a person.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Band>

  <CtaBand
    heading="Start with the one that hurts most"
    lede={SITE.promise}
    primary={{ label: 'Explore the products', href: '/product/' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'Talk to us', href: '/contact/' }}
  />
</MarketingLayout>
